otherwise. Current exceptions:

  skills/figure-table-audit/   Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial
  skills/citation-check/       4.0 International (CC BY-NC 4.0)

Both directories are adapted from Steven Denney's open-science-skills
(https://github.com/scdenney/open-science-skills, CC BY-NC 4.0), which in
turn remixes workflow concepts from Cheng-I Wu's Academic Research Skills
for Claude Code (CC BY-NC 4.0). They may not be used commercially, and
attribution must be preserved. See the attribution block at the end of each
SKILL.md and https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/ for the full
terms.

The per-field sweep in skills/citation-check/ additionally draws on Scott
Cunningham's bibcheck (https://github.com/scunning1975/MixtapeTools), which
is offered freely with attribution appreciated but not required. It adds no
license condition; the CC BY-NC restriction above comes from Denney and Wu
alone.

Everything else, including hooks/, rules/, settings/, and all README files,
